<article class="env-lemma" id="BA00D0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BA00D0">Lemma <span data-tag="BA00D0">3.2.1.9</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a simplicial set, $K' \subseteq K$ a simplicial subset, and $A$ a set of vertices of $K$. Let $\calE $ denote the set of all degenerate edges of $K \times \Delta ^1$, together with the edges $\{ a\}  \times \Delta ^1$ where $a \in A$. Let $B = (K' \times \Delta ^1) \coprod _{ K' \times \{ 1\}  } (K \times \{ 1\} ) \subseteq K \times \Delta ^1$. Suppose that, for every nondegenerate simplex $\sigma $ of $K$, either $\sigma $ belongs to $K'$, or the final vertex of $\sigma $ belongs to $A$. Then the inclusion </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (B, \calE \cap B_1) \subseteq (K \times \Delta ^1, \calE ) \]
</div>
  <p> is marked anodyne. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Working cell-by-cell, we reduce to Lemma <a href="/tag/DB7C30" data-tag="DB7C30">3.2.1.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>